# One step writes a note, a later one reads it in `with open(..) as f` and returns `f.read()`: `f` is bound to what
# `open` gives, and what is read goes back to `run`, which prints it. The note stands between the two steps.

route withopen.run
step run/save
step run/save/open                                          # `with open(NOTE, "w") as f`, as `f = open(..)`
step run/load
step run/load/open
line entry > run call
line run/save > File(data/note.txt) own
line File(data/note.txt) > run/load own
line run/load > run back                       # the note, a str
line run > Screen own
line run/save/open > TextIOWrapper·f@run/save/open value
line run/load/open > TextIOWrapper·f@run/load/open value
line TextIOWrapper·f@run/save/open > run/save value   # `f.write(..)`
line TextIOWrapper·f@run/load/open > run/load value   # `f.read()`
home TextIOWrapper·f@run/save/open run/save
home TextIOWrapper·f@run/load/open run/load

side entry left
side File(data/note.txt) between
side Screen right
